From: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:32:50 -0500
Subject: regulator: fixed: don't reject ACPI devices

Linux 7.3.6 added an early check to reg_fixed_voltage_probe():

	if (!pdev->dev.of_node && strcmp(pdev->name, "reg-fixed-voltage"))
		return -ENODEV;

A fixed regulator described in ACPI (PRP0001 with compatible
"regulator-fixed", configured by fwnode_get_fixed_voltage_config() from
0033-regulator-add-acpi-support) has no of_node and its platform device
is named after the ACPI device (PRP0001:0a), so every such regulator is
now rejected with -ENODEV.

On an Orange Pi 6 (ACPI boot) the NVMe slot's power switch is one of
them (\_SB.PVC0, "ssd2_power"), and sky1-pcie.2 stays deferred forever
("supplier PRP0001:0a not ready"), so the root file system on NVMe is
never found. All four fixed regulators on the board fail the same way.

Let devices with an ACPI companion through, as before.

Tested on an Orange Pi 6 (CIX P1, ACPI): with this, all four PRP0001
fixed regulators bind, the NVMe root port comes up and the board boots
from NVMe on v7.3.6 + patches-7.3.

Signed-off-by: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/regulator/fixed.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/fixed.c b/drivers/regulator/fixed.c
index c83a16246..ebe9a0c73 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/fixed.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fixed.c
@@ -269,7 +269,8 @@ static int reg_fixed_voltage_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	enum gpiod_flags gflags;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!pdev->dev.of_node && strcmp(pdev->name, "reg-fixed-voltage"))
+	if (!pdev->dev.of_node && !has_acpi_companion(&pdev->dev) &&
+	    strcmp(pdev->name, "reg-fixed-voltage"))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	drvdata = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(struct fixed_voltage_data),
-- 
